he command returned -- the pair collapsed into the promise the\n  callers already had. Both still *wait on the host*, though, and\n  their commands are `async` for that reason (US-070, US-080): the\n  engine one waits out a sidecar restart, and the external-player one\n  probes every place VLC might be, a process each. A synchronous\n  command would do either on the main thread with the window frozen\n  behind it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67494884-68da-4440-a200-b8d24d5f1da3","uuid":"5ac3676d-8467-43b1-97b4-3bf75af813cd","timestamp":"2026-10-13T05:24:32.397Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"67:## Rules every module follows\n69:- **Every export is `async`** (FR-10), including wrappers around\n72:- **No channel string reaches a caller.** One named function per\n75:- **Listener registration resolves to an unsubscribe function** and\n78:- **`ipc-os.js` and `ipc-engine.js` share no exports** (FR-9).\n87:- **`shell.js` owns `showItemInFolder`, `openPath` and\n101:- **Nothing here returns a Node object.** `fs.stat` resolves to a\n107:- **`fs.js` is backed by `fs/promises`, not `fs`.** Callback and\n112:## `cast.js` is the surface for work that has not happened (US-075)\n125:- **It is not in the unimplemented register**, because the *shim* is\n131:- **An empty answer can be the correct one.** Discovery reports no\n136:- **The event names are checked against the host by `cargo test`**,\n143:## `ipc-engine.js` is not an IPC module any more (US-044)\n164:- **Sends are queued until a socket is open**, then flushed in order.\n172:- **Subscriptions live in this module's own `handlers` map, never on the\n176:- **A dropped connection retries forever, with capped backoff**, and a\n185:## Implementation pattern (set by `ipc-os.js`, US-020)\n216:- **`menu.js` validates descriptors before it builds anything**\n222:## Gotchas\n247:- **`ipc-engine.js` is the exception to that glob.** Since US-046 it\n  therefore has the host send the whole list as an arra