{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfygPDoBpDp5Cgiqf56Su","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Six of the seven checklist items are done and committed. The last one, the full gate, is not ticked: `npm test` fails, though not because of anything this ticket changed.\n\n**Host (`7834d9a`):** the new `src-tauri/src/ready.rs` holds a `Readiness` record that starts not ready and becomes ready on the signal. A second signal, such as after a webview reload, is not an error. It has three unit tests. `main.rs` registers it as managed state and adds two commands: `ipc_ready` sets the record, and `state_saved` is only an acknowledgement. `is_ready()` has `#[allow(dead_code)]` because nothing reads it until US-065, and `clippy -D warnings` would reject it otherwise.\n\n**Renderer (`db8041e`):** `signalReady()` now calls the host's `ipc_ready`, and `signalStateSaved()` calls `state_saved`. Neither sends arguments and both resolve to `undefined`. The host's empty return arrives in the webview as `null`, so the tests make the stubbed `invoke` return `null` to show the caller still gets `undefined`. I removed both names from the stub register and changed its US-065 comment to list only the two dialogs. That shim change and the register edit are one commit, because committing the shim alone would have failed the stub sweep.\n\nI also added that `null` gotcha to `src/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md` (`dcadedf`).\n\n**The gate:** `npm test` stops at depcheck, which reports `nightralph` as an unused devDependency. That entry came in with the `nightralph init` commit (`b7d017b`), so I left `package.json` alone as out of scope. Every other stage passes:\n- the two lint steps\n- depcheck when `nightralph` is ignored\n- 4205/4205 unit tests\n- `cargo fmt --check`\n- `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo test`, 209/209\n\nSince you say the orchestrator runs `npm test` after I exit, it will probably reject the ticket until `nightralph` is added to depcheck's `--ignores` in the `test` script, or dropped from devDependencies.\n\n**Left for the other ticket in this spec:**\n- `onLog` and `onError`, and the register comment that names a nonexistent `log.rs`, are still untouched.\n- The startup test that checks `ipc_ready` arrives after the listeners register can't pass until those two stop throwing, so it belongs with that ticket.\n\nAll of this is in `.nightralph/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_read_input_tokens":82406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67494884-68da-4440-a200-b8d24d5f1da3","uuid":"a0c53bb5-c43f-4ac8-b77f-ceba390aee58","timestamp":"2026-10-13T05:25:17.210Z","request_id":"req_011CfygPDNNtY2BG4LwDBHtm"}
